{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"CimdPolicy","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Whether, and on what terms, a "},{"code":"client_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" that is a URL is resolved by fetching the document"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it names (T21.5, "},{"code":"draft-ietf-oauth-client-id-metadata-document","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"). # Why this is one nested","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"policy rather than nine fields Every field here is a term of a single decision — ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"do we"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fetch a stranger’s URL and make a client out of what comes back"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" — and none of them means","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"anything without [","type":"text"},{"code":"Self::enabled","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"]. A tenant that states a CIMD posture states all of it; a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tenant that states none inherits its organization’s whole posture rather than half of one,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which is the only merge that cannot produce a combination neither party wrote. # The two","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fields that can widen, and the seven that cannot [","type":"text"},{"code":"Self::enabled","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"] and [","type":"text"},{"code":"Self::allow_http","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"]","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"ordered"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": a tenant may turn either off but never on, exactly as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"dynamic_registration","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" may only move down its ladder. Everything else names ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"this tenant’s","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"domains or ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"this tenant’s","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" bounds, and there is no sense in which one tenant’s list of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"trusted publishers is stricter than another’s — the same argument [","type":"text"},{"code":"OidcPolicy","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"] already","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"makes for ","type":"text"},{"code":"dcr_allowed_redirect_hosts","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". # Every bound here is a security control","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"[","type":"text"},{"code":"Self::max_metadata_bytes","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"], [","type":"text"},{"code":"Self::min_cache_secs","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"] and [","type":"text"},{"code":"Self::max_cache_secs","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"] are not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tuning knobs. They are, respectively, the ceiling on a read from an attacker-chosen URL, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"floor under how often that read may be repeated, and the ceiling on how long its result may","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"be trusted. Each is clamped again in code against the three constants above, so a settings","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"row written by hand cannot lift them.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/cimdpolicy"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"struct","externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK10CimdPolicyV","modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"CimdPolicy","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Structure","title":"CimdPolic