y list is not a refusal of"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"everything, it is “loopback only”, which is exactly the Claude Code and VS Code profile.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/CimdPolicy\/trustedRedirectDomains","type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"trustedRedirectDomains","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"trustedRedirectDomains","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": [","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":"]?","kind":"text"}]},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/CimdPolicy":{"title":"CimdPolicy","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/CimdPolicy","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/cimdpolicy","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"CimdPolicy"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"CimdPolicy"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Whether, and on what terms, a "},{"code":"client_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" that is a URL is resolved by fetching the document"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it names (T21.5, "},{"code":"draft-ietf-oauth-client-id-metadata-document","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"). # Why this is one nested"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"policy rather than nine fields Every field here is a term of a single decision — "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"do we"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fetch a stranger’s URL and make a client out of what comes back"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — and none of them means"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"anything without ["},{"code":"Self::enabled","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"]. A tenant that states a CIMD posture states all of it; a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tenant that states none inherits its organization’s whole posture rather than half of one,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which is the only merge that cannot produce a combination neither party wrote. # The two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fields that can widen, and the seven that cannot ["},{"code":"Self::enabled","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"] and ["},{"code":"Self::allow_http","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"]"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"ordered"}]},{"type":"text","text":": a tenant may turn either off but never on, exactly as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"dynamic_registration","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" may only move down its ladder. Everything else names "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"this tenant’s","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"domains or "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"this tenant’s"}]},{"type":"text","text":" bounds, and there is no sense in which one tenant’s list of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"trusted publishers is stricter than another’s — the same argument ["},{"code":"OidcPolicy","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"] already"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"makes for "},{"code":"dcr_allowed_redirect_hosts","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". # Every bound here is a security control"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"["},{"code":"Self::max_metadata_bytes","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"], ["},{"code":"Self::min_cache_secs","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"] and ["},{"code":"Self::max_cache_secs","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"] are not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tuning knobs. They are, respectively, the ceiling on a read from an attacker-chosen URL, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"floor under how often that read may be repeated, and the ceiling on how long its result may"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"be trusted. Each is clamped again in code against the three constants above, so a settings"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"row written by hand cannot lift them."}]},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/CimdPolicy/trustedClientIDDomains":{"abstract":[{"text":"The hosts whose documents this tenant will fetch at all, as globs (","type":"text"},{"code":"mcp.example.com","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"*.example.com","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for every host under one domain). ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An empty list resolves nothing"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and enabling CIMD while it is empty is refused — see [","type":"text"},{"code":"validate_cimd_policy","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"]. That is a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"deliberate departure from “a URL is a client identifier, so any URL will do”: the fetch","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is triggered by an unauthenticated request naming the URL, so an unrestricted list is a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"request-forgery primitive offered to strangers, bounded only by the SSRF guard’s address","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rules. Naming the publishers a tenant actually fronts costs one settings field and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"removes the class. ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"*","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is refused here, and so is a wildcard over a whole top-level","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"domain","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"code":"*.com","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"): both are the posture the empty list is refused for, spelled","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"differently, and a control with no second control behind it cannot have a one-character","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"bypass and still be the control. It is a floor and not a public-suffix check —","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"*.github.io","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" passes, and trusting shared hosting stays the operator’s decision, bounded","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"by the per-tenant quota rather than by this field. ","type":"text"},{"code":"*","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" remains valid in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"[","type":"text"},{"code":"CimdPolicy::trusted_redirect_domains","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"], whose entries are not fetch targets.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"trustedClientIDDomains","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": [","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]?","kind":"text"}],"title":"trustedClientIDDomains","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/CimdPolicy\/trustedClientIDDomains","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/cimdpolicy\/trustedclientiddomains","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK":{"abstract":[{"text":"The official Swift SDK for AXIAM (Access eXtended Identity and Authorization Management).","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK","title":"AxiamSDK","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/CimdPolicy/minCacheSecs":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"minCacheSecs"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text"